{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.genus_maximal_descent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_maximal_descent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus_maximal_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_maximal_descent","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_maximal_descent.lean#L33-L52","doc":"**Genus from maximal descent** (manuscript claims (i)–(ii)).\n\nLet `(C, A, τ)` be a quantum observable universe satisfying the Descartes\ncondition `χ(A) = −6`.  If geometric descent produces a compact\none-complex-dimensional base `M₀`, then Riemann–Roch `χ = 2(1 − g)`\nforces the genus `g = 4` — the maximal genus consistent with the Hurwitz\nbound `|Aut(Σ_g)| ≤ 84(g − 1) = 252`.\n\n* (i) the genus is `4` — **derived** from `χ = −6` via Riemann–Roch;\n* (ii) the Hurwitz bound `aut_order ≤ 84 (g − 1)` holds (the standard\n  Hurwitz theorem, carried as the hypothesis `hhurwitz`).\n\n`χ`, the categorical Euler characteristic, and the Riemann–Roch identity\nare the genuine inputs; the genus value is computed, not assumed. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:genus-maximal-descent","label":"prop:genus-maximal-descent","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus_of_riemann_roch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_of_riemann_roch","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_maximal_descent.lean#L24-L31","doc":"Riemann–Roch on the descent curve `M₀`: `χ = 2(1 − g)` for the\ncategorical Euler characteristic `χ` and the genus `g`.  This is the\ngenuine geometric input — given it, the genus is determined. ","signatureChunk":0}]}